        "Notes": "The book contains a letter dated 16 April 1616 addressed to the printer Tommaso Baglioni. On the previous page one reads; `Girolamo Canini correggeva le stampe portategli a casa`. The first letter comments on the staging of Campeggi`s `Filarmindo`, while the second describes the staging of Campeggi`s `L`Aurora ingannata` on the occasion of the Riario-Pepoli wedding. The date of the second letter is fake.",
